<title>USA: Norwest Corp Q4 net rises. [CORRECTED 14:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Norwest Corp Q4 net rises. [CORRECTED 14:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.81		    $0.72</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$0.81		    $0.72</p>
<p> Net			308,100		  259,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 374,300		  352,700</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 interest income $1.61 billion vs $1.56 billion, non-interest income $738.1 million vs $522.3 million.  </p>
<p>Assets $80.18 billion vs $72.13 billion</p>
<p>Deposits $50.13 billion vs $42.03 billion</p>
<p>Net loans, leases $38.34 billion vs $35.24 billion</p>
<p>		     YEAR</p>
<p> Shr primary		$3.07		    $2.76</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$3.07		    $2.73</p>
<p> Net		    1,153,900		  956,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 369,700		  331,700</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 interest income $6.32 billion vs $5.72 billion.</p>
<p>1996 non-interest income $2.56 billion vs $1.85 billion.</p>
<p>1996 results are after (corrects from &quot;before&quot;) non-recurring, pretax charge of $19.0 million or $0.03 per diluted share for Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF) recapitalization assessment, recorded in third quarter.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
